{"beat": 17, "name": "THE CATHEDRAL", "text": "In 1912, Woolworth merged his company with his partners' chains: 596 stores. That year the company sold $60.6 million. And on April 24, 1913, President Wilson pressed a button in the White House and 80,000 lights came on in a tower on Broadway: 792 feet tall, the tallest building in the world until 1930. It cost $13.5 million. It was built without a mortgage, and by 1914 Woolworth owned it outright. A minister who saw it called it the Cathedral of Commerce. Woolworth said he built it to advertise his stores all over the world. It was paid for, nickel by nickel and dime by dime, by a price that hadn't moved. So far, the moral writes itself: find the price, hold the price.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "In", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.12}, {"word": "1912,", "start": 0.12, "end": 1.08}, {"word": "Woolworth", "start": 1.86, "end": 2.1}, {"word": "merged", "start": 2.1, "end": 2.5}, {"word": "his", "start": 2.5, "end": 2.66}, {"word": "company", "start": 2.66, "end": 3.08}, {"word": "with", "start": 3.08, "end": 3.3}, {"word": "his", "start": 3.3, "end": 3.44}, {"word": "partners'", "start": 3.44, "end": 4.02}, {"word": "chains:", "start": 4.02, "end": 4.38}, {"word": "596", "start": 5.02, "end": 5.82}, {"word": "stores.", "start": 5.82, "end": 6.44}, {"word": "That", "start": 7.28, "end": 7.44}, {"word": "year", "start": 7.44, "end": 7.64}, {"word": "the", "start": 7.72, "end": 7.78}, {"word": "company", "start": 7.78, "end": 8.1}, {"word": "sold", "start": 8.1, "end": 8.48}, {"word": "$60.6", "start": 8.48, "end": 9.92}, {"word": "million.", "start": 9.92, "end": 10.32}, {"word": "And", "start": 10.96, "end": 11.1}, {"word": "on", "start": 11.1, "end": 11.2}, {"word": "April", "start": 11.2, "end": 11.42}, {"word": "24,", "start": 11.42, "end": 12.08}, {"word": "1913,", "start": 12.48, "end": 13.38}, {"word": "President", "start": 14.22, "end": 14.46}, {"word": "Wilson", "start": 14.46, "end": 14.86}, {"word"